1
00:00:00,448 --> 00:00:18,465
The architecture is one API, one worker, and PostgreSQL. Signed HTTP acceptance commits first; asynchronous processing has its own durable history.

2
00:00:18,465 --> 00:00:36,474
Identity is source plus event ID. HMAC covers the exact timestamp and request bytes. Changed bytes under an existing identity are rejected rather than replacing history.

3
00:00:36,474 --> 00:00:52,867
A transaction combines the refund projection, processing receipt, completion ledger, attempt outcome, and inbox outcome. The guarantee covers these database-local effects.

4
00:00:52,867 --> 00:01:02,347
Now the normal worker is stopped. Owned test workers will be killed at real commit boundaries. These demonstrations use two-second leases; normal leases are thirty seconds.

5
00:01:02,347 --> 00:01:05,706
Before commit: no projection, processing receipt, or completion has committed. Killing the actual worker PID 7324 now.

6
00:01:05,706 --> 00:01:11,428
After commit: the processing receipt and one completion already exist. Killing the actual worker PID 24632 now.

7
00:01:11,428 --> 00:01:38,630
Before-commit termination rolled back all local effects. After lease expiry, recovery recorded an abandoned attempt and a successful second attempt, with one completion.

8
00:01:38,630 --> 00:02:02,831
After-commit termination preserved the completed transaction. A replacement worker processed a fresh probe, while this original event kept one attempt and one completion.

9
00:02:02,831 --> 00:02:24,920
The old owner paused after claiming. A replacement acquired the expired lease and committed. Resuming the old owner produced lost_lease and changed no committed outcome.

10
00:02:24,920 --> 00:02:39,936
The proof includes actual worker PIDs, barrier observations, database snapshots, and process logs. Run pnpm verify to repeat it; disposable services and secrets are removed afterward.

11
00:02:39,936 --> 00:02:52,052
Scope: synthetic events and one local database. External payments or network calls need their own idempotency protocol. This finite lab retains deduplication identities without expiry.
